386
00:43:15,532 --> 00:43:19,956
This is a component lead, not a jumper wire.

387
00:43:19,956 --> 00:43:23,350
One end goes to D1 cathode.

388
00:43:23,350 --> 00:43:27,099
The other end goes to BZ1 plus.

389
00:43:27,099 --> 00:43:31,133
Signal: flyback diode cathode.

390
00:43:31,133 --> 00:43:39,806
Status: provisional. Make it only after gate G11 have passed and you have recorded the results.

391
00:43:39,806 --> 00:43:45,065
Check: Band toward buzzer +.

392
00:43:45,065 --> 00:43:51,699
Node three is wired, except for the blocked transistor connections and the buzzer supply.

393
00:43:51,699 --> 00:44:04,407
The buzzer supply wire, N3-35, is installed only after the first power-up check, and only once the transistor is resolved.

394
00:44:04,407 --> 00:44:12,465
The bus is one straight line: end A at Node one, through Node two, to end B at Node three.

395
00:44:12,465 --> 00:44:21,603
A star or Y-shaped branch makes reflections that corrupt bits, so every node sits directly on the line with a short tap.

396
00:44:21,603 --> 00:44:33,216
The two terminators absorb the signal at the ends. Twist each CAN high and CAN low pair together, and run the ground wire beside it.

397
00:44:33,216 --> 00:44:36,695
Use your gate G6 readings now.

398
00:44:36,695 --> 00:44:46,268
If no module has an onboard terminator, fit RT1 at Node one and RT2 at Node three, exactly as shown.

399
00:44:46,268 --> 00:44:53,152
If the Node one or Node three module already has one, leave out that external resistor.

400
00:44:53,152 --> 00:44:59,976
If the Node two module has one, stop until it is removed.

