One end goes to the TRX1 pin printed CANL.

425
00:47:17,181 --> 00:47:22,040
The other end goes to the TRX2 pin printed CANL.

426
00:47:22,040 --> 00:47:26,754
Signal: CANL trunk, segment 1.

427
00:47:26,754 --> 00:47:35,307
Status: provisional. Make it only after gate G4 have passed and you have recorded the results.

428
00:47:35,307 --> 00:47:45,400
Check: Twist with B-01. Continuity TRX1 CANL to TRX2 CANL.

429
00:47:45,400 --> 00:47:48,335
Connection B-03.

430
00:47:48,335 --> 00:47:50,919
Take a black jumper.

431
00:47:50,919 --> 00:47:55,583
One end goes to the TRX1 pin printed GND.

432
00:47:55,583 --> 00:48:00,427
The other end goes to the TRX2 pin printed GND.

433
00:48:00,427 --> 00:48:05,216
Signal: GND reference, segment 1.

434
00:48:05,216 --> 00:48:13,769
Status: provisional. Make it only after gate G4 have passed and you have recorded the results.

435
00:48:13,769 --> 00:48:20,373
Check: Continuity Node 1 GND to Node 2 GND.

436
00:48:20,373 --> 00:48:23,307
Connection B-04.

437
00:48:23,307 --> 00:48:25,916
Take a yellow jumper.

438
00:48:25,916 --> 00:48:30,575
One end goes to the TRX2 pin printed CANH.

439
00:48:30,575 --> 00:48:35,419
The other end goes to the TRX3 pin printed CANH.

440
00:48:35,419 --> 00:48:41,417
Signal: CANH trunk, segment 2 (board A to B).

441
00:48:41,417 --> 00:48:49,970
Status: provisional. Make it only after gate G4 have passed and you have recorded the results.

442
00:48:49,970 --> 00:48:56,159
Check: Continuity TRX2 CANH to TRX3 CANH.

443
00:48:56,159 --> 00:49:04,238
This wire crosses from breadboard A to breadboard B. Keep it short and twisted with its partner.

444
00:49:04,238 --> 00:49:07,212
Connection B-05.

445
00:49:07,212 --> 00:49:09,761
Take a green jumper.

446
00:49:09,761 --> 00:49:14,435
One end goes to the TRX2 pin printed CANL.

447
00:49:14,435 --> 00:49:19,294
The other end goes to the TRX3 pin printed CANL.

448
00:49:19,294 --> 00:49:25,298
Signal: CANL trunk, segment 2 (board A to B).

449
00:49:25,298 --> 00:49:33,851
Status: provisional. Make it only after gate G4 have passed and you have recorded the results.

450
00:49:33,851 --> 00:49:42,594
Check: Twist with B-04. Continuity TRX2 CANL to TRX3 CANL.

451
00:49:42,594 --> 00:49:50,673
This wire crosses from breadboard A to breadboard B. Keep it short and twisted with its partner.

452
00:49:50,673 --> 00:49:53,747
Connection B-06.

453
00:49:53,747 --> 00:49:56,331
Take a black jumper.

454
00:49:56,331 --> 00:50:00,990
One end goes to the TRX2 pin printed GND.

455
00:50:00,990 --> 00:50:06,979
The other end goes to the bottom minus rail of breadboard B, which is ground.

456
00:50:06,979 --> 00:50:11,743
Signal: GND reference, segment 2.

457
00:50:11,743 --> 00:50:21,376
Status: provisional. Make it only after gates G4 and G14 have passed and you have recorded the results.

458
00:50:21,376 --> 00:50:28,299
Check: Continuity Node 2 GND to Node 3 GND rail.

459
00:50:28,299 --> 00:50:31,979
Connection N3-08.

460
00:50:31,979 --> 00:50:36,402
This is a component lead, not a jumper wire.

461
00:50:36,402 --> 00:50:44,486
One end goes to RT2, the 120 Ohm terminator, bus end B, end 1.

462
00:50:44,486 --> 00:50:49,330
The other end goes to the TRX3 pin printed CANH.

463
00:50:49,330 --> 00:50:53,878
Signal: CANH (end B terminator).

464
00:50:53,878 --> 00:51:03,491
Status: provisional. Make it only after gates G6 and G13 have passed and you have recorded the results.

465
00:51:03,491 --> 00:51:11,605
Check: Fit only if G6 found no onboard terminator on TRX3.

466
00:51:11,605 --> 00:51:15,399
Connection N3-09.

467
00:51:15,399 --> 00:51:19,823
This is a component lead, not a jumper wire.

468
00:51:19,823 --> 00:51:27,871
One end goes to RT2, the 120 Ohm terminator, bus end B, end 2.

469
00:51:27,871 --> 00:51:32,730
The other end goes to the TRX3 pin printed CANL.

470
00:51:32,730 --> 00:51:37,294
Signal: CANL (end B terminator).

471
00:51:37,294 --> 00:51:46,907
Status: provisional. Make it only after gates G6 and G13 have passed and you have recorded the results.

472
00:51:46,907 --> 00:51:55,840
Check: RT2 measured 114-126 Ohm before fitting.

473
00:51:55,840 --> 00:52:04,294
The bus is complete. There are two terminators, one at each physical end, and none at Node two.

474
00:52:04,294 --> 00:52:11,612
CAN high only ever meets CAN high, and CAN low only ever meets CAN low.

475
00:52:11,612 --> 00:52:20,066
With everything unplugged, check every wire against the ledger checklist, both ends, one row at a time.

476
00:52:20,066 --> 00:52:24,955
Tick a row only after you have looked at it and tested it with the meter.

477
00:52:24,955 --> 00:52:30,384
Every blocked row must be empty on the breadboard.

478
00:52:30,384 --> 00:52:35,343
Check the supplies for shorts, with all power removed.

479
00:52:35,343 --> 00:52:42,116
Measure from three volt three to ground on each node, and from Node three's VIN to ground.

480
00:52:42,116 --> 00:52:48,630
The reading may start low and climb as capacitors charge. That is normal.

481
00:52:48,630 --> 00:52:57,203
A steady reading near zero ohms is a short. Find it before any cable is plugged in.

482
00:52:57,203 --> 00:53:04,752
Check CAN high from Node one to Node two to Node three. It should read almost zero ohms.

483
00:53:04,752 --> 00:53:07,621
Do the same for CAN low.

484
00:53:07,621 --> 00:53:16,600
Then check that neither line connects to ground, a supply, or any ESP32 pin.

485
00:53:16,600 --> 00:53:20,879
Now measure CAN high to CAN low anywhere on the bus.

486
00:53:20,879 --> 00:53:32,101
Two 120 ohm resistors in parallel give 120 times 120 divided by 240, which is 60 ohms.

487
00:53:32,101 --> 00:53:41,729
About 120 means one terminator is missing. About 40 means there is a third, probably an onboard one.

488
00:53:41,729 --> 00:53:50,442
Record the value. Do not add resistors to fix a reading until you know why it is wrong.

489
00:53:50,442 --> 00:53:58,806
Last checks. GPIO thirteen must connect only to the base resistor, never to the buzzer.

490
00:53:58,806 --> 00:54:02,655
The buzzer's plus leg has no wire yet.

491
00:54:02,655 --> 00:54:07,319
VIN must have no wire to any three volt three point.

492
00:54:07,319 --> 00:54:14,917
And the three volt three pins of Node one and Node two must not be connected to each other.

493
00:54:14,917 --> 00:54:22,076
Power up one node at a time. The bus stays isolated from any vehicle or network.

494
00:54:22,076 --> 00:54:35,513
The other two nodes stay unplugged. TI's datasheet says an unpowered SN65HVD230 does not disturb the bus, so the bus wires can stay in place.

495
00:54:35,513 --> 00:54:43,862
Watch and feel for heat, smell or repeated resets. If you notice any, unplug at once.

496
00:54:43,862 --> 00:54:49,456
Never change a wire while a cable is plugged in.

497
00:54:49,456 --> 00:54:58,604
Plug in Node 1 only, and open a serial monitor at 115200 baud.

498
00:54:58,604 --> 00:55:06,057
The banner lines start with a hash sign. Look for CAN init OK, controller running.

499
00:55:06,057 --> 00:55:13,940
Measure the transceiver supply. It must be between three point zero and three point six volts.

500
00:55:13,940 --> 00:55:17,690
Then unplug it.

501
00:55:17,690 --> 00:55:26,838
Plug in Node 2 only, and open a serial monitor at 115200 baud.

502
00:55:26,838 --> 00:55:34,291
The banner lines start with a hash sign. Look for CAN init OK, controller running.

503
00:55:34,291 --> 00:55:42,174
Measure the transceiver supply. It must be between three point zero and three point six volts.

504
00:55:42,174 --> 00:55:52,887
Node two alone will report transmit errors, because no other node is powered to acknowledge its frames. That is expected at this stage.

505
00:55:52,887 --> 00:55:56,637
Then unplug it.

506
00:55:56,637 --> 00:56:05,780
Plug in Node 3 only, and open a serial monitor at 115200 baud.

507
00:56:05,780 --> 00:56:13,233
The banner lines start with a hash sign. Look for CAN init OK, controller running.

508
00:56:13,233 --> 00:56:21,116
Measure the transceiver supply. It must be between three point zero and three point six volts.

509
00:56:21,116 --> 00:56:33,004
On Node three, also measure VIN to ground. This is gate G12. It must be between four point four and five point two five volts.

510
00:56:33,004 --> 00:56:36,754
Then unplug it.

511
00:56:36,754 --> 00:56:40,468
Connection N3-35.

512
00:56:40,468 --> 00:56:43,132
Take a orange jumper.

513
00:56:43,132 --> 00:56:50,995
One end goes to ESP3 pin VIN: the first pin from the USB end on the VIN side header.

514
00:56:50,995 --> 00:56:54,745
The other end goes to BZ1 plus.

515
00:56:54,745 --> 00:57:00,279
Signal: 5V_USB_N3 (buzzer supply).

516
00:57:00,279 --> 00:57:09,816
Status: provisional. Make it only after gates G11 and G12 have passed and you have recorded the results.

517
00:57:09,816 --> 00:57:20,930
Check: Install LAST, with power off, after G12. No continuity from this wire to any 3V3 pin or rail.

518
00:57:20,930 --> 00:57:36,697
Today this wire stays OUT: the buzzer driver is blocked until the transistor is identified. Install it later only with all power off, after G10, G11 and G12 pass.

519
00:57:36,697 --> 00:57:41,046
A successful compile only proves the code built.

520
00:57:41,046 --> 00:57:49,479
When Node two prints sent CAN ID, the frame was queued. That alone does not prove it reached the bus.

521
00:57:49,479 --> 00:57:59,977
The evidence is another node printing a frame line with that CAN ID, while the error counters stay low and no bus-off alert appears.

522
00:57:59,977 --> 00:58:06,486
Plug in Node one, then Node two. Node three stays unplugged.

523
00:58:06,486 --> 00:58:12,885
On Node one's serial monitor, look for lines of JSON with type frame.

524
00:58:12,885 --> 00:58:23,813
You should see CAN IDs 0x201, 0x202 and 0x203 about once a second, and 0x210 twice a second.

525
00:58:23,813 --> 00:58:30,376
Node one acknowledges the frames, so Node two's transmit errors should stop.

526
00:58:30,376 --> 00:58:40,390
Write down exactly what you see. If nothing arrives, unplug everything and go to the troubleshooting table.

527
00:58:40,390 --> 00:58:48,398
Now plug in Node three. Nothing is rewired, and both terminators stay at the two ends.

528
00:58:48,398 --> 00:58:55,621
Node three's monitor firmware is listen-only. It should print the same frame IDs.

529
00:58:55,621 --> 00:59:07,554
The OLED, LEDs and buttons will do nothing yet, because no firmware drives them. That is expected, not a fault.

530
00:59:07,554 --> 00:59:15,068
Here is the finished build. Compare all three nodes and the bus with the manual one last time.

531
00:59:15,068 --> 00:59:22,906
Photograph each node and the whole bus, and keep the photos with the sign-off sheet.

532
00:59:22,906 --> 00:59:26,311
To be clear about what has been tested.

533
00:59:26,311 --> 00:59:37,408
The documents, the pin ledger and the firmware pin settings were checked against each other. No hardware was inspected, measured or powered by Claude.

534
00:59:37,408 --> 00:59:44,577
Each gate, the 60 ohm reading and the frame capture become verified only when you record them.

535
00:59:44,577 --> 00:59:52,545
The transistor connections and the buzzer supply are still blocked, and the peripheral firmware still has to be written.

536
00:59:52,545 --> 00:59:57,079
Thank you for building carefully.
